Wire the assessment to the live Cal.com booking link

The event type exists and is configured: cal.com/ownertwin/25-minutes-no-pitch,
25 minutes, Cal Video, four booking questions.

  What kind of business is it?        required, short text
  How many people, including you?     required, select
  Your Owner Gap result               optional, select, identifier "result"
  What is eating your week right now? required, long text

Cal prefills a booking question from a URL param named after its identifier,
so READY now links to ?result=READY and their score lands in the form already
filled. Verified on the live booking page: the dropdown reads READY without
them touching it.

Cal's stock "Additional notes" field was turned off. It duplicated the fourth
question and asked the same thing twice with a vaguer label.

Only READY gets the calendar. WRITTEN DOWN gets an email link carrying its
score in the subject. ONE OF A KIND and OUT OF THE WAY get no CTA at all,
which is the filter working rather than a gap.

EMAIL moved to hello@ownertwin.com now that the mailbox exists.

Buttondown URLs deliberately untouched. That account is still named FRAMEZERO
and changing the site first would break the form for everyone.

All four result paths re-verified headless. No JS errors.

